        "date": "2026-11-20T20:21:29Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(import): refuse STEP items with no length-unit context\n\nThe second review of PR #2927 found two paths around the unit-context\nrefusal. A solid that no representation lists, and a piece that the\ntopology reader splits from a surface model, had no context in the unit\nindex, so the reader took 1 mm per unit without a word.\n\nThe unit index now gives each split piece the context of its model, as\nthe reader does (topology::items). When the file states a length unit,\nan item with no context is refused by name, the same as an item whose\ncontext states no unit. A file with no length unit keeps the mm default.\n\nPins (crates/kernel/tests/step_short_units.rs):\n- solid_listed_by_no_representation_is_refused\n- split_surface_model_pieces_in_unitless_context_are_refused\n- split_surface_model_pieces_in_inch_context_keep_scale (control)\n\nRefs #2919\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
